      "text": "To find the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\), we start by solving the equation for \\(x\\).\n\nFirst, we take the square root of both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n(x - 5)^2 = 9\n\\]\n\\[\nx - 5 = \\pm 3\n\\]\nThis gives us two separate equations to solve:\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n\\]\n\nSolving the first equation:\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 3 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 8\n\\]\n\nSolving the second equation:\n\\[\nx - 5 = -3\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -3 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 2\n\\]\n\nThe roots of the equation are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\). To find the sum of the roots, we add them together:\n\\[\n8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of the roots is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
